  "rationale": "`assets/skills/habeas-requirements/SKILL.md` is a bundled skill with front matter, so it is a site of `requirements.cli.skill_conventions`. Its front-matter description says when to use the skill in terms of the user's task. That is \"during design sessions and before changing code, tests, or requirement text in a Habeas project\", including when the user only asks for a feature, bug fix, CLI flag, test, dependency bump, or wording tweak. This meets the MUST. It also points to `habeas-refactor` for moving code or requirements and to `habeas-evidence` for validation findings. The requirement's MAY permits this, so it is not a gap. No violation matches were listed, and no gap was found.",
